cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this environment or its findings, please cite it as below."
title: "transformer-repair-gym: a GPU-free RL environment for multi-file transformer debugging"
abstract: >-
  A verifiable reinforcement-learning environment in which a policy must localize and
  repair real defects in a small transformer training repository. Grading is
  execution-based and runs behind a trusted-comparator boundary: the container that
  executes candidate code holds no reference implementation, no hidden checks and no
  serialized reference data, and returns observations rather than verdicts. The
  accompanying evidence records the three successive isolation failures (R14, R15, R16)
  that produced that design, including the measurements that falsified the first two.
authors:
  - name: "Rance"
license: MIT
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/rance/transformer-repair-gym"
keywords:
  - reinforcement learning
  - verifiable rewards
  - reward hacking
  - program repair
  - transformers
  - evaluation
